{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791661998,"nonce":"fQAEkCCdFukEtEf+xP+NrYcNX0k=","title":"Containers: host preflight and per-secret Quadlet drop-ins","message":"Spec 018 rev 2 section Moving to containers (ticket C13, split out of C6). jobhunter container preflight runs on the host (refuses in container mode): creates missing data and cache dirs at 0700 and an empty config.toml if absent; checks ownership; finds files under the data and cache dirs whose SELinux type is not container_file_t once the dirs are labelled and prints the chcon command (never runs it); refuses to pass while host timers from jobhunter schedule install are enabled; warns when ~/.config/jobhunter/gmail_token.json or google_client_secret.json still exist after the podman secrets do and prints the rm line (never deletes); compares jobhunter version on the host with the image label (C12); reads podman secret ls (names only) and writes one Quadlet drop-in per existing secret per unit following the least-privilege matrix in spec 018, so no unit names a secret that does not exist; prints the install commands. Uses the host-escape chain (flatpak-spawn --host, distrobox-host-exec) when podman is not on PATH. Checks without podman: pytest with fake podman, systemctl and ls outputs, drop-in golden files, and a test that each drop-in names only secrets in the fake podman secret ls; if /usr/libexec/podman/quadlet exists, run it with -dryrun -user on the generated tree and assert success (skip otherwise); ruff and pytest. Needs the user on the host: jobhunter container preflight prints all ok and the listed drop-ins.","files":null}]}